Actually you can, some of them.
The values of some of the options are saved in the save file, and the
other options are read from the personal config file every time a saved
game is started. 
(Of course, when a new game is started, all the options are read from the
config file. And the ones not defined there get their default values.)

People who have the source can check include/flag.h :
the options defined in struct flag are saved in the save files, and
options defined in struct instance_flags are not. The instance_flags are
the ones always read from the config file on restoring.

